{"black_box_warning":{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","fda_source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"],"proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The no-boxed-warning conclusion is supported, but the current row cites DailyMed for the boxed-warning field, which is not permissible under the audit policy. Use the FDA/openFDA label API metadata instead.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect"},"blocking_questions":[],"fact_checks":[{"current_value":"methsuximide","field":"generic_name","proposed_value":"methsuximide","rationale":"FDA labeling identifies Celontin as methsuximide capsules, USP.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"mesuximide","rationale":"NCBI LiverTox states methsuximide is also called mesuximide. This alias should be captured to avoid duplicate-row treatment.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Celontin; Methsuximide","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Celontin","rationale":"Celontin is the proprietary/brand name; methsuximide is the established generic name already captured in generic_name, not a separate trade name.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Celontin","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Celontin; mesuximide","rationale":"Mesuximide is a documented alternate name and should be included as a search alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Yes","field":"available_in_us","proposed_value":"Yes","rationale":"FDA sources show Celontin NDA 010596 and an FDA-approved/marketed generic methsuximide capsule ANDA 217213.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.fda.gov/drugs/generic-drugs/competitive-generic-therapy-approvals","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"Oral capsule","field":"formulations_available","proposed_value":"Oral capsule","rationale":"FDA labeling describes methsuximide as capsules for oral use.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Absence","field":"epilepsy_type","proposed_value":"Absence","rationale":"FDA labeling indicates Celontin for control of absence (petit mal) seizures refractory to other drugs.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA labeling states methsuximide suppresses the 3-cycle-per-second spike-wave activity of absence seizures and reduces attack frequency apparently by depression of motor cortex and elevation of CNS seizure threshold.","field":"mechanism_of_action","proposed_value":"FDA labeling states methsuximide suppresses the 3-cycle-per-second spike-wave activity of absence seizures and reduces attack frequency apparently by depression of motor cortex and elevation of CNS seizure threshold.","rationale":"This matches FDA label clinical pharmacology language.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Moderate","field":"mechanism_confidence","proposed_value":"Moderate","rationale":"The FDA label uses mechanistic but qualified language, supporting a moderate rather than high-confidence assignment.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling","rationale":"The mechanism is supported by FDA labeling; DailyMed should not be the named source when FDA/accessdata and openFDA sources are available.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"1200 mg/day in selected FDA label dosage schedule.","field":"maximum_approved_daily_dose","proposed_value":"1200 mg/day in selected FDA label dosage schedule.","rationale":"FDA labeling gives escalation to a daily dosage of 1.2 g, equivalent to 1200 mg/day. The deterministic mismatch appears to be a unit-format false positive.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Suggested schedule: 300 mg/day for first week, then increase by 300 mg/day weekly if needed to 1200 mg/day per FDA label.","field":"typical_doses_per_day","proposed_value":"Suggested schedule: 300 mg/day for first week, then increase by 300 mg/day weekly if needed to 1200 mg/day per FDA label.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports 300 mg/day for week 1, weekly 300 mg/day increases, and a target daily dosage of 1.2 g.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"300 mg/day initial labeled dose; optimal dose individualized to seizure control with tolerable adverse effects.","field":"minimum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"300 mg/day initial labeled dose; optimal dose individualized to seizure control with tolerable adverse effects.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the 300 mg/day initial dose and individualized optimal dosing language.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A 0%: FDA label lists nausea/vomiting, anorexia, diarrhea, weight loss, epigastric/abdominal pain, constipation, drowsiness, ataxia/dizziness, irritability/nervousness, headache, blurred vision, photophobia, hiccups, insomnia, confusion, depression, psychosis, urticaria, SJS, rash, and blood dyscrasias without quantified incidence percentages.","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"N/A: FDA labeling reports adverse reactions without incidence percentages. Listed reactions include GI symptoms, hematologic abnormalities/blood dyscrasias, neurologic and sensory symptoms, psychiatric abnormalities including rare psychosis/suicidal behavior/auditory hallucinations, dermatologic reactions including Stevens-Johnson syndrome, hyperemia, proteinuria/microscopic hematuria, and periorbital edema.","rationale":"The current statement is directionally supported but the '0%' prefix is misleading and the list omits several labeled adverse reactions.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS; Dermatologic; GI; Hematologic; Neurologic; Psychiatric","field":"filter_symptom_category","proposed_value":"CNS; Dermatologic; GI; Hematologic; Neurologic; Psychiatric; Cardiovascular; Genitourinary; General/Other","rationale":"FDA labeling also lists hyperemia, proteinuria/microscopic hematuria, and periorbital edema.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA label does not define clinically meaningful enzyme induction or inhibition; label notes possible increases in phenytoin and phenobarbital concentrations.","field":"enzyme_inducing_or_inhibiting","proposed_value":"N/A - selected FDA label does not define clinically meaningful enzyme induction or inhibition; label notes possible increases in phenytoin and phenobarbital concentrations.","rationale":"FDA labeling notes possible increases in phenytoin and phenobarbital concentrations. PubMed PMID 6403891 also reports significant rises after methsuximide addition, but does not classify methsuximide as an inducer or inhibitor.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not provide a half-life value; label notes an active N-desmethylmethsuximide metabolite in overdose.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Active metabolite N-desmethylmethsuximide: accumulation half-life 49.7 hours and elimination half-life 72.2 hours in PubMed PMID 6403891; FDA labeling notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide in overdose but does not provide half-life.","rationale":"The FDA label caveat is true, but a trusted PubMed pharmacology source provides half-life values for the principal plasma substance/active metabolite, so N/A is incomplete.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not identify a major metabolic organ; label notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide metabolite and advises liver/renal caution.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic/liver; NCBI LiverTox states methsuximide is metabolized in the liver via the cytochrome P450 system (CYP3A4). FDA labeling notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide in overdose and advises liver/renal caution.","rationale":"The label-only limitation is true, but NCBI provides a trusted source for hepatic metabolism.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"missing","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic","rationale":"NCBI LiverTox identifies liver metabolism via CYP3A4, so the filter should not remain limited/unknown.","requires_user_approval":true,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"No QT interval effect described in selected FDA label.","field":"qt_interval_effect","proposed_value":"No QT interval effect described in selected FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The selected FDA label does not describe QT effects; this supports a label-absence statement, not an affirmative QT study result.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Approved February 8, 1957 (NDA 010596; predates Jan 1, 1982).","rationale":"FDA accessdata approval correspondence states Celontin was approved on February 8, 1957; this is more exact than the current pre-1982 wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010596s022ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book pre-1982 succinimide ASM; FDA-labeled for absence (petit mal) seizures refractory to other drugs.","field":"status_or_notes","proposed_value":"FDA-approved succinimide ASM for absence (petit mal) seizures refractory to other drugs; NDA 010596 was originally approved February 8, 1957; generic methsuximide capsule ANDA 217213 was approved/first marketed May 1, 2023.","rationale":"FDA labeling supports the indication; FDA accessdata and CGT approvals provide exact approval/availability context.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010596s022ltr.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/generic-drugs/competitive-generic-therapy-approvals"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling and approval correspondence; FDA CGT approvals list; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed PMID 6403891","rationale":"DailyMed should not be used as the named FDA source for the boxed-warning field, and additional trusted sources are needed for aliases, metabolism, and half-life.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"missing_source","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010596s022ltr.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/generic-drugs/competitive-generic-therapy-approvals","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","rationale":"The warning conclusion is supported, but the source wording must be changed from DailyMed to FDA/openFDA.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; published=Apr 09, 2026; title=CELONTIN (METHSUXIMIDE) CAPSULE [PARKE-DAVIS DIV OF PFIZER INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; effective_time=20260407; title=Celontin / METHSUXIMIDE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","rationale":"DailyMed is impermissible for black-box verification under the row audit policy; FDA/openFDA is acceptable.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"incorrect","supporting_sources":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"pubmed_phase_ii_iii_rct_links","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT of methsuximide was identified. The key PubMed clinical pharmacology/efficacy publication located for methsuximide was not placebo-controlled.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=methsuximide+placebo+randomized+trial","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/"]},{"current_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was retained in the PubMed RCT audit/gap review as of 05-19-2026; RCT section set to N/A per current scope.","field":"rct_pubmed_verification_notes","proposed_value":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled randomized epilepsy RCT was identified in PubMed searches for methsuximide/mesuximide/Celontin; RCT section remains N/A.","rationale":"Searches did not identify a qualifying placebo-controlled RCT. Available clinical reports are uncontrolled/open-label or non-placebo designs.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=(methsuximide+OR+mesuximide+OR+Celontin)+placebo+randomized+trial+epilepsy","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]}],"generic_name":"methsuximide","missing_rcts":[],"outcome_checks":[{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_50_responder_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT was identified, so differential RR50 is not available.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=(methsuximide+OR+mesuximide+OR+Celontin)+placebo+randomized+trial+epilepsy"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_median_pct_change_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT was identified, so differential median percent seizure reduction is not available.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=(methsuximide+OR+mesuximide+OR+Celontin)+placebo+randomized+trial+epilepsy"]},{"current_value":"N/A","field":"diff_seizure_freedom_maximum_effective_dose","proposed_value":"N/A","rationale":"No qualifying phase II/III placebo-controlled RCT was identified, so differential seizure freedom is not available.","requires_user_approval":false,"status":"verified","supporting_sources":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/?term=(methsuximide+OR+mesuximide+OR+Celontin)+placebo+randomized+trial+epilepsy"]}],"overall_status":"needs_update","proposed_row_updates":[{"current_value":"","field":"alternate_generic_names","proposed_value":"mesuximide","reason":"Documented NCBI alias.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Celontin; Methsuximide","field":"trade_names","proposed_value":"Celontin","reason":"Methsuximide is the generic name, not a separate trade name.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Celontin","field":"pubmed_search_aliases","proposed_value":"Celontin; mesuximide","reason":"Add documented alternate name for literature searches.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"mechanism_source","proposed_value":"FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling; FDA/openFDA labeling","reason":"Use trusted FDA sources directly rather than DailyMed wording.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"N/A 0%: FDA label lists nausea/vomiting, anorexia, diarrhea, weight loss, epigastric/abdominal pain, constipation, drowsiness, ataxia/dizziness, irritability/nervousness, headache, blurred vision, photophobia, hiccups, insomnia, confusion, depression, psychosis, urticaria, SJS, rash, and blood dyscrasias without quantified incidence percentages.","field":"adverse_symptoms_percentages","proposed_value":"N/A: FDA labeling reports adverse reactions without incidence percentages. Listed reactions include GI symptoms, hematologic abnormalities/blood dyscrasias, neurologic and sensory symptoms, psychiatric abnormalities including rare psychosis/suicidal behavior/auditory hallucinations, dermatologic reactions including Stevens-Johnson syndrome, hyperemia, proteinuria/microscopic hematuria, and periorbital edema.","reason":"Avoid misleading '0%' wording and include omitted labeled adverse reactions.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"CNS; Dermatologic; GI; Hematologic; Neurologic; Psychiatric","field":"filter_symptom_category","proposed_value":"CNS; Dermatologic; GI; Hematologic; Neurologic; Psychiatric; Cardiovascular; Genitourinary; General/Other","reason":"FDA labeling includes hyperemia, urinary findings, and periorbital edema.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not provide a half-life value; label notes an active N-desmethylmethsuximide metabolite in overdose.","field":"half_life_range","proposed_value":"Active metabolite N-desmethylmethsuximide: accumulation half-life 49.7 hours and elimination half-life 72.2 hours in PubMed PMID 6403891; FDA labeling notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide in overdose but does not provide half-life.","reason":"Trusted PubMed source provides active-metabolite half-life values.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"N/A - selected FDA/DailyMed label does not identify a major metabolic organ; label notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide metabolite and advises liver/renal caution.","field":"major_organ_for_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic/liver; NCBI LiverTox states methsuximide is metabolized in the liver via the cytochrome P450 system (CYP3A4). FDA labeling notes active N-desmethylmethsuximide in overdose and advises liver/renal caution.","reason":"NCBI source identifies hepatic metabolism.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf"]},{"current_value":"Limited/unknown","field":"filter_metabolism","proposed_value":"Hepatic","reason":"NCBI LiverTox supports hepatic metabolism.","requires_user_approval":true,"source_urls":["https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/"]},{"current_value":"Approved Prior to Jan 1, 1982 (FDA Orange Book)","field":"year_fda_cleared","proposed_value":"Approved February 8, 1957 (NDA 010596; predates Jan 1, 1982).","reason":"FDA accessdata approval correspondence provides the exact original approval date.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010596s022ltr.pdf"]},{"current_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current DailyMed label.","field":"fda_black_box_warning","proposed_value":"No FDA boxed warning identified in selected current FDA/openFDA label.","reason":"DailyMed is not permissible for boxed-warning verification; FDA/openFDA is.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; published=Apr 09, 2026; title=CELONTIN (METHSUXIMIDE) CAPSULE [PARKE-DAVIS DIV OF PFIZER INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; effective_time=20260407; title=Celontin / METHSUXIMIDE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","reason":"Replace impermissible DailyMed boxed-warning source with FDA/openFDA source.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5"]},{"current_value":"FDA Orange Book products file; FDA/DailyMed labeling","field":"evidence_sources","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA labeling; FDA Drugs@FDA/accessdata labeling and approval correspondence; FDA CGT approvals list; NCBI LiverTox; PubMed PMID 6403891","reason":"Add trusted sources for FDA label facts, FDA approval/availability, alias/metabolism, and half-life; remove DailyMed as named source.","requires_user_approval":false,"source_urls":["https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/label/2010/010596s22lbl.pdf","https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/drugsatfda_docs/appletter/2010/010596s022ltr.pdf","https://www.fda.gov/drugs/generic-drugs/competitive-generic-therapy-approvals","https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK548535/","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/6403891/"]}],"rct_link_checks":[],"source_updates":[{"current_value":"FDA/DailyMed SPL; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_label; setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; published=Apr 09, 2026; title=CELONTIN (METHSUXIMIDE) CAPSULE [PARKE-DAVIS DIV OF PFIZER INC]; url=https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74","field":"fda_black_box_warning_source","proposed_value":"FDA/openFDA drug label API; status=no_boxed_warning_in_selected_fda_label; spl_set_id=64a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74; effective_time=20260407; title=Celontin / METHSUXIMIDE; api_url=https://api.fda.gov/drug/label.json?search=openfda.spl_set_id%3A%2264a6ee88-c6b1-4e13-8208-b6772ef65a74%22&limit=5","reason":"Black-box verification must use FDA/openFDA